{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789298439,"nonce":"lTlZmjF5T+sDW8V/jCAplHzibzA=","title":"Let a host register a native library's resolver by name","message":"A .hl that declares natives of a library ash cannot find on disk fails at\nload (\"Required library 'caribou' not found\"). NativeFunctionResolver\nresolves a native only from a dlopen'd Library through the DEFINE_PRIM\nresolver protocol, keyed by library name, and the runtime seam\n(std/src/rt.rs) has no slot for native resolution.\n\nA host that provides natives from inside the process, caribou binding\nHaxe @:hlNative(\"caribou\", ...) methods to bridge calls on objects of\nanother language, needs to register a library without a file:\n`hlp_rt_register_native_library(name: *const c_char, resolve: unsafe\nextern \"C\" fn(name: *const c_char, sign: *mut *const c_char) -\u003e *mut\nc_void)`. discover_and_load_libraries treats a registered name as found;\nresolve_function_uncached asks the registered resolver before dlsym; the\nresolver follows the DEFINE_PRIM contract (writes the signature string,\nreturns the function). Default: no registered libraries, so ash alone is\nunchanged.\n\nCompanion (caribou-side, no ash change): the Haxe class the build macro\nemits is an ordinary class with @:hlNative methods and an\nhl.Abstract\u003c\"caribou_obj\"\u003e handle field; `extern class` is refused by the\nHL target (\"Extern type not supported\").","files":null}]}